          "kicker": "Form tracker",
          "heading": "Fiji concede an average of 29.6 points across their last 11 matches",
          "body": "Fiji have conceded 326 points in total across their last 11 games. This defensive record averages out to 29.6 points conceded per match over that 11-game span. At the other end of the pitch, the team scored 315 points over the same 11-game period, maintaining an average of 28.6 points per fixture. The brightest point of this 11-match sequence remains the home test in September 2025, where they achieved their biggest victory of the window by beating Canada 63-10 in the Pacific Nations Cup knockout stage."
        }
